    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (the others are a base and a helper). The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `Idempotency-Key` support for `POST /api/owners` so a repeated create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which the existing duplicate-identity rule would otherwise reject with 409).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (no controllers, no `@Transactional`; escalations for error/branch responses), I added:\n\n**New functions** (`rest/function/owner/`)\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new first step of the pipeline. Reads only the `Idempotency-Key` header (via OfficeFloor's `@HttpHeaderParameter`, leaving the request body free for the existing `NormalizeOwnerAddress` to bind once). If the key was already used, it throws `IdempotentReplayException(ownerId)` to short-circuit before any validation/duplicate checks.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new step right after `SaveOwner`, once the owner has its generated id. Records `key \u2192 ownerId`. No-op when no key is sent.\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a `@Component` singleton wrapping a `ConcurrentHashMap<String,Integer>` (`putIfAbsent`, first-writer-wins), shared across requests.\n\n**New escalation** (`rest/escalation/` + YAML)\n- `IdempotentReplayException` (checked) and `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler`, which re-loads the owner by id and responds **200** with the mapped `OwnerDto` \u2014 mirroring the codebase's `DuplicateIdentityException` handler pattern rather than using `@Flow` branching.\n\n**Wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted `checkIdempotency` as the entry step (`next: normalizeAddress`) and `recordIdempotency` between `save` and `audit` (under the same `transaction` governance span).\n\nA request with no key, or an unseen key, flows through the normal create pipeline unchanged \u2014 so all existing behavior is preserved. `./mvnw -o test` is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), including the new `coreIdempotentRepeat` checkpoint.",
