    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, exactly as the code wires it. The pipeline entry point is `checkIdempotency`, and every step runs inside `govern: [ transaction ]` (except the idempotency pre-check), so it all commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; without it the request is rejected before any step runs.\n\n## Pipeline, in execution order\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** *(side-effect / short-circuit)* \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header only. If that key already produced an owner, throws `IdempotentReplayException` (returns the original owner, 200) instead of creating a duplicate. No key / unseen key falls through.\n\n2. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect \u2014 reads body once)* \u2014 binds `@RequestBody` OwnerFieldsDto (the only step that reads the body). If `addressLine1` is non-blank, uses the structured form: normalizes line1/line2 (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations), sets line2 to null if empty, and composes the flat `address` from them. Otherwise normalizes the flat `address`. Republishes the DTO as a variable for later steps.\n\n3. **RequireOwnerFields** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`, 400) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank, listing every offending field. (Address is checked *after* normalization.)\n\n4. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** *(validation)* \u2014 postcode optional; when present must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in that inclusive range. Else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n5. **ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate** *(validation)* \u2014 `registrationDate` optional; if supplied it must not be after today, else `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n\n6. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps country code after a leading `+`, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`. Result must be 8\u201315 digits; and national length must match the country code (+61 \u2192 9 digits, +1 \u2192 10). Writes back E.164 form in place; invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n\n7. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 email optional; when present, lower-cases it in place and validates syntax against a regex, else `InvalidEmailException` (400).\n\n8. **RejectDisposableEmailDomain** *(validation)* \u2014 if the (already lower-cased) email's domain is in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), rejects with `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n9. **CheckUniqueOwnerIdentity** *(validation)* \u2014 computes the deterministic householdId (`SHA-256(normalizedLastName|postcode)`) and identity key (`telephone|email|householdId`). Scanning all non-soft-deleted owners: rejects (`DuplicateIdentityException`, 409) on an exact identity-key match, or on a shared household (same lastName+postcode) unless the request set `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n10. **CheckOwnerCityCapacity** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects (`CityAtCapacityException`, 409) if the request's city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed).\n\n11. **CheckDailyOwnerLimit** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects (`DailyOwnerLimitException`, 429) if \u2265 100 owners already have today's business-day (weekend rolled forward to Monday) as `registrationDate`.\n\n12. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the validated/normalized DTO into a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`.\n\n13. **AssignOwnerHousehold** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName|postcode)` (matches the value used in step 9).\n\n14. **DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets the effective registration date: supplied date or today, then rolls weekends forward to Monday (business day).\n\n15. **AssignOwnerCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, REGION derived from postcode (NSW/VIC/QLD/UNKNOWN), HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of `SHA-256(telephone + lastName)`. On collision with an existing code, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) to stay unique.\n\n16. **AssignOwnerMembershipNumber** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the fiscal year (starting 1 July) of the registration date.\n\n17. **AssignOwnerNamesakeCount** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of already-stored owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive), not counting itself.\n\n18. **AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 defaults `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. If not a declared household member and a postcode exists, and some non-deleted owner shares lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but has a different telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = that owner's id.\n\n19. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via the repository (assigns its id).\n\n20. **RecordIdempotencyKey** *(side-effect)* \u2014 records the `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 new owner id in the store (no-op if no key was sent), enabling replay by step 1.\n\n21. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 logs an `AUDIT` line with the owner's id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel and membershipNumber.\n\n22. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect / response)* \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, sets a `bulkSignupWarning` (from `DailyOwnerRegistrations`), and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notes\n- Steps 1 and 20\u201322 read the `Idempotency-Key` header; only step 2 reads the request body (bound once).\n- `membershipLevel` in the audit/response is a derived field computed by `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, not a stored pipeline assignment.\n- All checks/assignments over \"existing owners\" iterate `ownerRepository.findAll()`; soft-deleted owners are skipped in the duplicate checks (steps 9 and 18) but *not* in city-capacity, namesake, or customer-code uniqueness scans."
